TITLE Geochemistry Question - No Redox
SOLUTION 1
    units mol/kgw
    temp 150
    pH 7
    pe 4
    water 1
GAS_PHASE 1
    -fixed_pressure
    -pressure 1
    -temperature 150
    CH4(g) 10
    CO2(g) 10
    NH3(g) 5
END
# To disable redox, we can use the "mass balance" on components.
# But in phreeqc.dat, CH4(g) is C(-4), CO2(g) is C(4), NH3(g) is N(-3).
# They are already separate in terms of their master species except for the redox.
# If we don't have an oxidant, they might not react anyway.
# But in my simulation, they DID react. (N(-3) went to N(0)).
# Let's try to use a database or settings that disable redox.
# Actually, the simplest way is to use "SOLUTION_SPECIES" to remove the redox reactions.
# But that's complicated.
# Let's try to just use a very low initial pe, or high pe, and see if it matters.
